+
+## (2) Continuity
+
+**Entry and prior-movement join.** Chapters 28–29 and the closed Movement 4 ledger hand off cleanly. The pin is d133; the Fiske bout is d141; Lira is on the top line with hip and shoulder costs carried; Cael's Compression forearm recovers on the fourth morning; five fragments are confirmed; Brom finishes the fourth exercise of the week on d141. Chapter 30 enters with Seln's private file on d143 and Cael's d144 observation of two-and-two rotations, the repaired ninth exercise, the recovered forearm, and “Six weeks … fewer now.” No state resets at the join.
+
+**Calendar and counts.** The current prose supports d143 private file, d144 counter/council, d147 first unit and night one, d148 night two, the reach around the third hour of the d149 night/early d150, d154 Wind misfire, and d167 birthday. The final/evaluation countdown is the coordinator's amended sixteen/seventeen days. Brom's count and the operation's sleep ledger reconcile as listed in section (1).
+
+There is one closeout-ledger residue, not a manuscript contradiction. The prose says the first leak occurs on “the ninth morning after the stair”; its next two leaks occur on the next afternoon and next morning, and the weekly Third-day unit meets “that afternoon.” With the early-d150 stair, that places the leaks on d159, d160, and d161, followed by the d161 unit; the moving trials remain d163 and the fifteenth-day coursework d164. The stale author-end-state table inside the pending Movement 5 block lists d158–160. Per the ledger's own rule that surviving prose governs plans, closeout should carry d159–161.
+
+**Capabilities and bodies.** Cael moves from five confirmed fragments plus the uncounted anomaly to six plus the anomaly. Shadow is Bronze, sustained, partial, directed, adversarial/non-combat, and settles outside the Iron read. Presence suppression and movement masking remain mutually exclusive in his hands; deliberate use fails; idle rent produces three near-collisions; deployment remains none. The Wind misfire occurs a little over ninety-six hours after the stair, self-corrects inside the next run, and is followed by three clean days before intensity. Lira's hip and shoulder, Cael's forearm and collarbone, attention fatigue, and the eight-day deferral all carry without disappearance.
+
+**Knowledge boundaries.** Lira, Brom, and Karis know the mechanism and the sixth acquisition. Nobody institutional does. Seln knows Cael occupied the gallery and stair but never looks down the flight, never learns the mechanism, and never learns that Cael acquired anything. Gwen knows only public rumor and “records business.” Jessup's client remains unidentified. The official record keeps five fragments.
+
+**Protected wording and reserved truths.** The fragment notice is exact in wording, line order, punctuation, tier, two-component note, and engagement field. The mapped anchors remain exact at their first use, including “Your file says you watch things well…,” “Sign me up,” “An instrument doesn't change sides…,” “A position is an argument…,” the Iron-tier-force/Karis Log, the complete Sixth-fragment Log, both assessment-office lines, Brom's furniture speech, *see holder*, Hesk's note, “Filed under debts…,” and “Still open. Still real. Patience.” The amended closing Log is exact. Seln's age fallback remains “since his Kindling.” The private case reveals no contents; the listening-system line is used once and filed as unknown; no maker, will, reset, classification falsification, Level 4 origin, or `[UNBOUND]` disclosure enters the movement.
+
+**Source and later canon.** The expanded movement preserves source chapters 12–14's event spine while the diagnostic finds 0 unprotected shared runs of eight or more words. Book 5's opening canon remains supported: Cael is sixteen with six confirmed fragments, one unreproduced/unaccounted anomaly, Shadow unknown to the record, and Seln still unaware of the mechanism and acquisition. No later-book dependency is broken.
