+## (4) Reader clarity
+
+**Speaker attribution.** The four-person council remains easy to assign by voice and action: Lira states and tests, Karis qualifies and records, Brom grounds the reasoning in conduct, and Cael reads and decides. The unit, records-hall response, wash-house trials, and birthday table all preserve explicit handoffs. No ambiguous speaker requires a line fix.
+
+**Referents and one-pass flow.** The repair removes the main recursive drag in chapters 30–31 and gives `rule two` an immediate antecedent. The three records-hall approaches remain spatially legible: gallery, service stair, half-landing, upper flight, archive door. Chapter 36 now clearly separates accidental idle drift, the ladder's mundane redirection of attention, and the fragment's failed deliberate activation. `Six`, `the read`, `the moving half`, `ordinary`, and `rent` keep stable referents.
+
+**Fluent thirteen-year-old lens.** The institutional reasoning is still the movement's most demanding material, but every abstraction is tied to an object or action: the chained pen, carbon sheets, unchanged coats, proud drawer, counting lock, loose ninth step, ladder, signed minute, and four-part plan. The operation and training problem can be understood without first mastering the paperwork vocabulary. The younger-reader entry remains denser than the action middle, but no new explanatory repair is needed.
+
+**Reader Standard.** Pass. Automated gates are zero. The language is clean; suspense and limited violence carry consequence without gore. Cael records desire and cost before acting, tells the people entitled to know, accepts stop rules, identifies probable theft as theft, refuses to interfere with the intruder, and records that preparation makes the outcome manageable rather than safe. Seln resolves the confrontation through restraint, law, witnesses, and paper.
+
+## (5) Listening proof
+
+Every chapter and every changed region was checked on the page and by ear. Straight quotation marks and emphasis asterisks are even by line and by chapter. The chapter 34 notice's two code fences are balanced. `git diff --check` reports no whitespace fault. The numeral scan finds only chapter headings and chapter 36's written `0`, immediately voiced in the next scene as “Nought”; no abbreviation requires expansion. Past/present `read`, ordinary/Path `Wind`, and the written `minute` are syntactically cued. Dialogue interruptions at em dashes are complete and audible.
+
+- **Chapter 30 — PASS.** 84 quotation marks, 36 asterisks, 4 correctly spaced breaks. The repaired audit joins and trap/no-trap compression retain subjects and hierarchy by ear. The chapter 29→30 join carries the pin, Fiske countdown, forearm, top line, and Brom count cleanly.
+- **Chapter 31 — PASS.** 236 quotation marks, 48 asterisks, 4 correctly spaced breaks. Four speakers remain attributable. The added minute/rule-two orientation is audible, and the shortened Log has no broken join.
+- **Chapter 32 — LINE FIX.** 158 quotation marks, 26 asterisks, 4 breaks. Quotes, italics, numerals, and joins pass, but the break after “a second mark on the stair” has no blank line above it. In CommonMark this can bind the sentence to the `---` as a setext heading instead of rendering a scene break.
+- **Chapter 33 — LINE FIX.** 72 quotation marks, 48 asterisks, 4 breaks. The sleep addition joins cleanly and the operation is audible, but the break before “At the half of the fourth hour” lacks its following blank line.
+- **Chapter 34 — PASS.** 34 quotation marks, 58 asterisks, 4 correctly spaced breaks, and a balanced fenced notice. Positions, speaker turns, the five-finger rule check, and the notice read cleanly. Brackets around `[unnamed]` may be silent in narration.
+- **Chapter 35 — PASS.** 208 quotation marks, 40 asterisks, 4 correctly spaced breaks. The shortened mechanic statements leave no fragment or doubled explanation. The seven-hour total, Wind misfire, comparison, and number seventeen remain audible in sequence.
+- **Chapter 36 — PASS.** 140 quotation marks, 82 asterisks, 5 correctly spaced breaks. The ladder clarification prevents the zero count from sounding like successful deployment. `0` is a visual field count, not an abbreviation; Seln's spoken “Nought” supplies the intended reading. The rent, aimed/not-aimed trials, moving-half failures, hazard, and debt keep distinct referents.
+- **Chapter 37 — PASS.** 126 quotation marks, 74 asterisks, 4 correctly spaced breaks. The board countdown, birthday speakers, pear-fork story, note, inventory, anomaly, amended evaluation countdown, and final letter all read cleanly. No homograph or broken closing join remains.
+
